# Bombay Plague Bayesian Model — Project README

This documents the current state of the pipeline after the round of prior-sensitivity
and sampler-robustness work that revised the model comparison. **Read the "Which files
are final" section before running or citing anything in `results/`.**

---

## 1. The one-paragraph summary

The manuscript's original LHS/AIC screening found the **constant** and **humidity-only**
β_H formulations best-supported, with **all-climate** essentially unsupported. A full
Bayesian re-analysis reversed this: **all-climate is now decisively best-supported**
(ΔlogZ ≥ 22.98 over the next-best model, confirmed independently by AICc and BIC). The
reversal traces to two concrete, fixed problems: (1) the original LHS/AIC bounds on
`aR`/`a0` structurally excluded the all-climate model's true optimum, and (2) a nested-sampling
convergence failure (fixed by switching `rwalk`→`rslice` and seeding a known-good live
point) that initially masked whether `betaH0`'s prior was truncating the posterior. Both
fixes are independently verified — see Section 4.

---

## 2. Which files are FINAL — use these, and only these, for the paper

| What | File |
|---|---|
| **Fitting script** | `scripts/run_final_all_models_v2.py` |
| **Posteriors (all 4 models)** | `results/final_model_comparison_v2/nested_sampling/{model}__plague_deaths_reported_fit__final_v2.pkl` |
| **Model comparison table** | `results/final_model_comparison_v2/final_model_comparison_v2.csv` |
| **Prepared data** | `prepared_data/merged_target_climate.csv` (via `scripts/prepare_data.py`) |
| **Best-fit parameter table** | generated by `scripts/make_supp_best_fit_table.py` → `results/final_figures/supp_best_fit_comparison_reported.{csv,tex}` |
| **Prior-ranges table** | generated by `scripts/make_supp_prior_table.py` → `results/final_figures/supp_prior_ranges.{csv,tex}` |
| **Climate-coefficient posteriors** | `scripts/final_climate_effects.py` — **⚠ currently points at the WRONG directory, see Section 5 before using** |
| **4-panel model-fit figure (credible band + MLE + median)** | `scripts/make_bayesian_model_fits_figure.py` → `results/final_figures/bayesian_model_fits/` |
| **Spillover/human decomposition** | `scripts/final_transmission_dynamics.py` → `results/final_figures/transmission_dynamics/` (run against `final_model_comparison_v2`) |
| **Spillover-reseeding robustness** | `scripts/check_spillover_reseeding_robustness.py` + `scripts/sweep_gamma_reseeding_falsification.py` |

**Do not use** `results/nested_sampling/`, `results/final_model_comparison/` (no `_v2`
suffix), or `model_comparison_bayesian.csv` at the results root — all three are earlier,
superseded generations (see the timeline in Section 4).

